✔ RUNZ1-KILL real live original holds slot, then reaped fixed scope gives receiptless Q exactly once (84.206858ms)
✔ RunControl real contract: readonly status, byte logs, stdin EOF, normal and nonzero native result (187.211626ms)
✔ normal exit 0 creates one durable final receipt before adoption (199.642269ms)
✔ cancel authenticates intent, returns promptly, preserves duplicate grace and signals three stages (156.123636ms)
✔ unknown scope refuses receipts, control and recovery after short shell without harness identity (156.792645ms)
✔ configuration claim leaves preserve user argv and only override four named leaves (0.597901ms)
✔ supervisor death receiptless Q uses registered stamp, no replacement execution or writer files (1955.901166ms)
✔ two real supervisors compete for one fake slot/ticket: loser touches no logs, exactly one submission (458.432856ms)
✔ registration commit before meta crash retains all stamp fields; missing/mismatched domain never backfills (2.053145ms)
✔ reconcile revision prevents competing cancel or registration being overwritten (1.018933ms)
✔ verified shell harness keeps native unknown separately from actual shell status 137 (378.055695ms)
✔ direct harness killed by a real signal records sourced wait signal (70.955522ms)
✔ accepted cancellation with verified scope absent never signals a guessed shell group (350.302106ms)
✔ orphan policy reacts to verified physical parent death, while continue preserves the run (200.335382ms)
